      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of a 58-year-old male with acute aortic dissection is presented. A few months earlier the patient underwent transmyocardial laser revascularisation and implantation of venous graft to the left anterior descending coronary artery due to three-vessel disease. Acute aortic dissection was successfully treated by surgery. Therapeutic options in patients with acute aortic dissection and advanced coronary artery disease are discussed."},
